- Ensure adequate personnel, equipment and resources are available to support preparedness and response operations.

Coordinate the development of multi-hazard early warning systems and risk reduction

- Coordinate implementation of the Multi-Hazard Early Warning System (MHEWS) Roadmap and divisional activities under the Early Warnings for All (EW4All) Initiative;

- Strengthen coordination between hazard monitoring agencies, emergency responders and communities to support end-to-end early warning systems;

- Support implementation of the Common Alerting Protocol (CAP) and warning dissemination arrangements;

- Coordinate hazard, vulnerability and risk assessments, risk profiling and preparedness planning;

- Support development of hazard maps, evacuation plans and warning protocols'

- Promote impact-based forecasting, anticipatory action and community feedback mechanisms to improve warning effectiveness.

Coordinate community resilience training and stakeholder engagements

- Coordinate Community-Based Disaster Risk Management (CBDRM) training programmes and community resilience initiatives across the Division;

- Support communities to prepare, review and test Community Disaster Risk Management Plans;

- Promote inclusive participation of women, youth, and persons with disabilities, older persons and vulnerable groups in disaster risk management;

- Coordinate community awareness, risk communication and behavioral change programmes;

- Strengthen partnerships with Government agencies, Provincial Councils, Municipal Councils, NGOs, OPDs, faith-based organizations, traditional leaders, development partners and the private sector;

- Facilitate Divisional, Provincial, Municipal, District and Community Disaster Risk Management Committee meetings and stakeholder consultations.

Coordinate emergency operations and response

- Support the Divisional Commissioner in coordinating disaster preparedness, response, relief and recovery operations;

- Coordinate activation and management of the Divisional Emergency Operations Centre (DEOC);

- Coordinate operational information management, situation reporting and inter-agency response;

- Facilitate Initial Damage Assessments (IDA), Post-Disaster Needs Assessments (PDNA) and recovery planning;

- Coordinate emergency logistics, resource mobilization and humanitarian assistance;

- Provide regular operational updates to the National Coordinator and National Emergency Operations Centre.

Conduct monitoring, evaluation and reporting

- Monitor implementation of DRM programmes, projects and Annual Work Plans within the Division;

- Collect, analyze and report performance data against national and donor indicators;

- Support operation of the National DRR Monitoring and Evaluation Online Tracker;

- Prepare monthly, quarterly, annual and post-disaster reports;

- Document lessons learned, after-action reviews, resilience case studies and best practices;

- Support reporting requirements for GCF, UNDP and other development partners.

Provide capacity development

- Coordinate disaster risk management training and capacity-building programmes for Government agencies, Provincial Administrations, community leaders and volunteers;

- Deliver training on Community-Based Disaster Risk Management, Emergency Operations, Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems and disaster preparedness;

- Coordinate simulation exercises, emergency drills and Training-of-Trainer programmes;

- Lead Early Warnings for All (EW4All) and Common Alerting Protocol (CAP) awareness programmes;

- Promote anticipatory action approaches and strengthen institutional and community preparedness.

The incumbent performs other duties within their functional profile as deemed necessary for the efficient functioning of the Office and the Organization. This includes supporting the implementation of special projects and national priorities related to disaster risk management, climate resilience and emergency management.

